1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,739
Same button. Two people.

2
00:00:02,189 --> 00:00:11,320
One of them is the chief engineer and one of them is a surgeon, and the ship can tell the difference.

3
00:00:11,770 --> 00:00:15,683
Last time a choice asked what your job is.

4
00:00:16,133 --> 00:00:19,611
This time it asks how good you are.

5
00:00:20,811 --> 00:00:22,550
One new line each.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,783
Skills, colon, then a list: a word, a number, a comma.

7
00:00:28,233 --> 00:00:30,841
The chief: engineering four, science one.

8
00:00:31,291 --> 00:00:33,900
The doctor: medical four, science three.

9
00:00:34,350 --> 00:00:43,480
The word is the name of the skill and you can invent your own, as long as it is one word.

10
00:00:43,930 --> 00:00:46,974
The number is how good they are.

11
00:00:47,424 --> 00:00:51,337
I use a scale that tops out at four.

12
00:00:51,787 --> 00:01:01,787
Two means you do it for a living, and here is something the game gives you for nothing: a job counts as two.

13
00:01:02,237 --> 00:01:06,585
The chief was already engineering two before I typed anything.

14
00:01:07,035 --> 00:01:09,209
Now look at the doctor.

15
00:01:09,659 --> 00:01:11,398
Her job is medical.

16
00:01:11,848 --> 00:01:14,022
Science is not her job.

17
00:01:14,472 --> 00:01:17,080
She is just good at it.

18
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:23,063
Lint is happy, and that is all there is to it.

19
00:01:23,513 --> 00:01:28,296
The game reads these numbers with the rest of the roster.

20
00:01:28,746 --> 00:01:32,224
I do not open the other file today.

21
00:01:32,674 --> 00:01:41,370
One thing worth knowing: the numbers belong to the person on the roster, not to the name on the screen.

22
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:52,254
If a player has saved a name of their own and sits in the doctor's chair, they are still as good as the doctor.

23
00:01:53,454 --> 00:01:58,672
On the bridge, a new choice. if skill science, at least three.

24
00:01:59,122 --> 00:02:03,904
Four parts: the word skill, which skill, a sign, a number.

25
00:02:04,354 --> 00:02:08,702
The doctor has science three, so she is offered it.

26
00:02:09,152 --> 00:02:12,630
The chief has science one, and is not.

27
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:16,559
And here is the difference from last time.

28
00:02:17,009 --> 00:02:22,661
When a job is missing from the party, one console covers for it.

29
00:02:23,111 --> 00:02:25,285
Nobody covers for a skill.

30
00:02:25,735 --> 00:02:31,822
If the doctor stays on the ship, the sensor record is on nobody's menu.

31
00:02:32,272 --> 00:02:35,315
So a skill choice is a bonus.

32
00:02:35,765 --> 00:02:39,243
Never put the only way forward behind one.

33
00:02:40,443 --> 00:02:42,183
Now the other kind.

34
00:02:42,633 --> 00:02:46,546
No if at all, so everyone is offered it.

35
00:02:46,996 --> 00:02:49,604
After the semicolon: check engineering 9.

36
00:02:50,054 --> 00:02:55,707
The game rolls a number from one to ten and adds your engineering.

37
00:02:56,157 --> 00:03:02,678
Nine or more, it works, and the party goes to the room in the brackets.

38
00:03:03,128 --> 00:03:07,911
Then else, and the room for when it does not work.

39
00:03:08,361 --> 00:03:19,665
So this one choice needs two rooms, and I write the failure as carefully as the success, because half my players are going to read it.

40
00:03:20,115 --> 00:03:23,159
Last part: a comma, and learn lockout.

41
00:03:23,609 --> 00:03:29,261
Anything after the check, after a comma, only happens when the check worked.

42
00:03:29,711 --> 00:03:34,059
The odds: target nine, skill four, six times in ten.

43
00:03:34,509 --> 00:03:36,683
Skill zero, two in ten.

44
00:03:37,133 --> 00:03:38,437
Twelve is hard.

45
00:03:38,887 --> 00:03:40,191
Six is easy.

46
00:03:41,391 --> 00:03:42,391
Four rules.

47
00:03:42,841 --> 00:03:45,450
A skill choice is a bonus.

48
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:50,248
A check has an else, and both rooms lead back.

49
00:03:50,698 --> 00:03:55,046
Before the check always happens, after it only on success.

50
00:03:55,496 --> 00:04:01,148
And the numbers go with the seat, whatever the player calls themselves. Lint.

51
00:04:01,598 --> 00:04:02,902
A misspelled Skills.

52
00:04:03,352 --> 00:04:07,700
A missing comma: it tells me that entry is dropped.

53
00:04:08,150 --> 00:04:14,237
A check with no number: nothing would be rolled, and it would always work.

54
00:04:14,687 --> 00:04:28,165
An else that points at a room I never wrote: that one would end the visit, and only on a failed roll, so I would not find it by playing once.

55
00:04:28,615 --> 00:04:39,920
And if science at least three, with the word skill left out: science on its own is a job, and a job is one or zero.

56
00:04:40,370 --> 00:04:42,543
Lint reads all of these.

57
00:04:42,993 --> 00:04:50,820
Two things it cannot know: a skill you misspelled on the roster itself, and a number nobody has.

58
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:53,020
The bridge.

59
00:04:53,470 --> 00:04:56,078
The doctor has the sensor record.

60
00:04:56,528 --> 00:04:59,137
The chief does not. The reactor.

61
00:04:59,587 --> 00:05:00,891
The doctor tries.

62
00:05:01,341 --> 00:05:06,124
There is her roll: engineering zero, and the board stays dark.

63
00:05:06,574 --> 00:05:08,748
The chief tries. Engineering four.

64
00:05:09,198 --> 00:05:24,850
That four is the number I typed on the roster, and that is the thing to look for: if it says two, that person's Skills line is not being read, and lint will tell you why.

65
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:27,039
Now the chief alone.

66
00:05:27,489 --> 00:05:31,402
The suit tags arrive marked as covering for medical.

67
00:05:31,852 --> 00:05:35,330
The sensor record does not come to anyone.

68
00:05:36,530 --> 00:05:39,574
Your third crew member gets two skills.

69
00:05:40,024 --> 00:05:46,111
Give them a choice only they can see and a check anyone can try.

70
00:05:46,561 --> 00:05:57,430
Then break it on purpose: take the s off one Skills, read what lint says, and play it once to see what that person loses.

71
00:05:57,880 --> 00:06:03,533
Next time, one of these people gets a quest that is theirs alone.
